# Clippy and formatting

Finish Rust changes only when both commands pass from `backend/` with no warnings:

```
cargo fmt --check
cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings -D clippy::unwrap_used -D clippy::expect_used
```

`clippy::unwrap_used` and `clippy::expect_used` are restriction lints, so `-D warnings` alone does not enforce them. Fix the finding in the code. An `#[allow(clippy::...)]` needs a comment on the line above naming the false positive. Do not use `#[allow(dead_code)]` or `#[allow(unused)]` to hide unfinished work.
